      "immutable": false,
      "summary": "run-verification skill: say how to wait for a background runner",
      "body": "Step 2 told the managing agent to start 'pipeline.py run' in the background but not how to wait for it. A verification-loop session improvised 'while pgrep -f \"pipeline.py run\"; do sleep 10; done' and an 'until ! pgrep -f ...' loop; each matched its own command line, so the session hung for 8 minutes after the runner had finished, until it was killed by hand at 19:49. Step 2 now says to wait for the background task's completion notification or poll 'pipeline.py status' until it shows 'running: 0', and never to wait with pgrep -f on a pattern. A documentation change only; checked that 'status' prints a 'running:' line.",
